  'Carnegie gave $62,500 in 1905 (New England Carnegies says he first meant it for a biology building), and Lord & Hewlett designed the library in the Italian Renaissance style. Enlarged in 1937, named in 1946 for President William Allan Neilson, given wings in 1962 and rededicated in 1982. Maya Lin\'s rebuilding, opened on March 29, 2021, kept the 1909 core and replaced the later wings.',
